  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.4.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: vrs\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - # Retain the revision pinned by the v0 recipe rather than changing source content during migration.\n    git: https://github.com/facebookresearch/vrs.git\n    rev: 89d9ec5f1867cb139d06eb7d297ef1206ad35478\n    patches:\n      # Remove after a VRS release includes https://github.com/facebookresearch/vrs/pull/263.\n      - patches/0001-use-conda-deps-in-cmake-config.patch\n  # Match the Ocean revision pinned by VRS's FetchContent declaration, but\n  # provide it as a recipe source so builds do not require GitHub access.\n  - url: https://github.com/facebookresearch/ocean/archive/5fca1d27a9f37e868738b6db09a6b1e00723d80f.tar.gz\n    sha256: c47c2bf97909cf35133d865bc59382f1bdb2d2c22c4583671d62d8666130aa43\n    target_directory: ocean\n\nbuild:\n  number: 14\n  script:\n    - if: unix\n      then: bash \"${RECIPE_DIR}/build.sh\"\n    - if: win\n      then: call \"%RECIPE_DIR%\\\\build.bat\"\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - cmake\n    - if: not win\n      then: ninja\n  host:\n    - libboost-devel\n    - rapidjson\n    - fmt\n    - libjpeg-turbo\n    - portaudio\n    - xxhash\n    - zlib\n    - qt\n    - qt-main\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - libgl-devel\n        - mesalib\n    - libpng\n    - lz4-c\n    - zstd\n    # Dependencies introduced by VRS 1.4.0.\n    - eigen\n    - libopus\n    - ffmpeg ${{ ffmpeg }}.* lgpl_*\n  run:\n    # The installed vrslib CMake config resolves these targets for consumers.\n    - libboost-devel\n    - rapidjson\n    - fmt\n    - libjpeg-turbo\n    - xxhash\n    - zlib\n    - libpng\n    - lz4-c\n    - zstd\n    - eigen\n    - libopus\n    - ffmpeg ${{ ffmpeg }}.*\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"vrs\", upper_bound=\"x.x\") }}\n\ntests:\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n        - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n        - cmake\n        - ninja\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - run_cmake_test.sh\n        - run_cmake_test.bat\n        - tests/\n    script:\n      - if: unix\n        then: bash run_cmake_test.sh\n      - if: win\n        then: call run_cmake_test.bat\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/facebookresearch/vrs\n  repository: https://github.com/facebookresearch/vrs\n  summary: A library and binaries for manipulating VRS files\n  description: |\n    VRS is a file format optimized to record & playback streams of sensor data, such as images, audio samples, and any other discrete sensors (IMU, temperature, etc), stored in per-device streams of timestamped records.\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jeongseok-meta\n    - SeaOtocinclus\n",
